<title>UK: RESEARCH ALERT - Pernod cut at Lehman.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT - Pernod cut at Lehman.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>French drinks group Pernod-Ricard was cut to &quot;underperform&quot; from &quot;outperform&quot; at Lehman Brothers, the investment bank said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Lehman analyst John Wakeley said he saw minimal earnings growth from the company, whose diversification into non-alcoholic areas was a poor use of excess capital, and little upside in the share price.</p>
<p>Pernod shares were diwb 0.5 percent at 305.0 francs by 1326 GMT.</p>
<p>-- David Holmes, London Newsroom +44 171 542 4367</p>
</text>
